# No UI borders

Personal Voice UI is **borderless**. Separate surfaces with background contrast, spacing, radius, and shadows — never with strokes.

## Do not

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
border: 1px solid #344252;
border-bottom: 1px solid #24303c;
border-color: #88d8c1;
box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #2a3644; /* faux border */
```

```tsx
/* ❌ BAD */
style={{ border: "1px solid …" }}
className="… border border-…"
```

## Do

```css
/* ✅ GOOD — fill + radius, optional soft shadow */
background: #111820;
border-radius: 8px;
box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
```

- Prefer `border: 0` (or omit borders) on buttons, inputs, menus, cards, panels, tooltips, and overlays.
- Focus/active: use `outline` or a background change — not `border` / `border-color`.
- `border-radius` and `box-sizing: border-box` are fine.
- When editing existing CSS, remove leftover visible `border*` / faux-border shadows in the same change.
